{"html":"<p>A lot of Java code used to be boilerplate: fields, a constructor, getters, <code>equals</code>, <code>hashCode</code> and <code>toString</code> for a class that only holds two numbers. Modern Java (17 and 21) gives three tools that make data modeling short and safe: records, enums and sealed types.</p>\n<h2 id=\"records-data-without-boilerplate\">Records: Data Without Boilerplate</h2>\n<p>A <strong>record</strong> is a class whose job is to hold data:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">record</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Point</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> x, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> y) {}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>That one line gives you:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>private final</code> fields <code>x</code> and <code>y</code>,</li>\n<li>a constructor <code>new Point(1, 2)</code>,</li>\n<li>accessors <code>x()</code> and <code>y()</code> (no <code>get</code> prefix),</li>\n<li><code>equals</code> and <code>hashCode</code> based on the values,</li>\n<li>a readable <code>toString</code>: <code>Point[x=1, y=2]</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">Point</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> p</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Point</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(p.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">x</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());                      </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 1</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(p.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">equals</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Point</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)));  </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// true</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Because <code>equals</code> and <code>hashCode</code> compare values, records work perfectly as map keys and in sets.</p>\n<p>Records are <strong>immutable</strong>: there are no setters. To &quot;change&quot; one, create a new one:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">Point</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> moved</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Point</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(p.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">x</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 5</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, p.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">y</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Point[x=6, y=2]</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h3 id=\"validation-in-a-compact-constructor\">Validation in a Compact Constructor</h3>\n<p>A record can check and clean its values in a <strong>compact constructor</strong>, written without parameters:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">record</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Email</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String value) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">    Email</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (value </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">==</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> null</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> ||</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> !</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">value.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">contains</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"@\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">            throw</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> IllegalArgumentException</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"invalid email: \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> value);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        value </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> value.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">trim</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">toLowerCase</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    String </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">domain</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> value.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">substring</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(value.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">indexOf</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">'@'</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>new Email(&quot;  Ana@Example.com &quot;)</code> stores <code>ana@example.com</code>, and <code>new Email(&quot;nope&quot;)</code> throws. Every <code>Email</code> in your program is now valid, so code receiving one never needs to check again. Records can have methods too, like <code>domain()</code>.</p>\n<p>What records can&#39;t do: extend another class, or have extra instance fields. They&#39;re for data, not for objects with changing state.</p>\n<h2 id=\"enums-a-fixed-set-of-values\">Enums: A Fixed Set of Values</h2>\n<p>An <strong>enum</strong> lists every possible value of a type:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">enum</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Status</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> { </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">PENDING</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">PAID</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">SHIPPED</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">Status</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> s</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Status.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">valueOf</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"PAID\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(s </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">==</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Status.PAID);   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// true</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Enums are safer than string constants: a typo like <code>Status.PAYED</code> doesn&#39;t compile, and <code>switch</code> can check that you handled every value. Compare them with <code>==</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"enums-with-fields-and-methods\">Enums With Fields and Methods</h3>\n<p>Each value can carry data, set through a constructor:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">enum</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Plan</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">    FREE</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">3</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">), </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">PRO</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">9</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">50</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">), </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">TEAM</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">29</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">500</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> final</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> monthlyPrice;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> final</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> maxProjects;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">    Plan</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> monthlyPrice</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> maxProjects</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">        this</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">.monthlyPrice </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> monthlyPrice;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">        this</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">.maxProjects </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> maxProjects;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    int</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> monthlyPrice</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() { </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> monthlyPrice; }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    boolean</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> allows</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> projects</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) { </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> projects </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> maxProjects; }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>Plan.PRO.monthlyPrice()</code> is <code>9</code>, and <code>Plan.FREE.allows(5)</code> is <code>false</code>. The rules live with the values, not in <code>if</code> chains spread around the code.</p>\n<p><code>EnumMap</code> and <code>EnumSet</code> are fast, ordered collections made for enum keys.</p>\n<p>Don&#39;t store <code>ordinal()</code> (the position number) in a database: adding a value in the middle changes every number after it. Store <code>name()</code> instead.</p>\n<h2 id=\"sealed-types-a-closed-set-of-classes\">Sealed Types: A Closed Set of Classes</h2>\n<p>An enum&#39;s values are fixed objects. Sometimes you need a fixed set of <strong>types</strong>, each with its own data. That&#39;s a <strong>sealed</strong> interface (Java 17):</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">sealed</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> interface</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Payment</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> permits</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> Card</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">BankTransfer</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">Voucher</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">record</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Card</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String last4) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">implements</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> Payment</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">record</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> BankTransfer</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String iban) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">implements</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> Payment</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">record</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Voucher</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String code, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> cents) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">implements</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> Payment</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>permits</code> lists every allowed implementation. No other class can implement <code>Payment</code>, so the compiler knows all the cases.</p>\n<h2 id=\"putting-it-together-pattern-matching\">Putting It Together: Pattern Matching</h2>\n<p>With sealed types and records, <code>switch</code> can handle every case, and take records apart with <strong>record patterns</strong> (Java 21):</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">static</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> String </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">describe</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(Payment payment) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    return</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> switch</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (payment) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        case</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Card c </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"card ending \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> c.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">last4</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        case</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> BankTransfer t </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"transfer from \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> t.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">iban</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        case</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Voucher</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String code, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> cents) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"voucher \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> code </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \" for \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> cents </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \" cents\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    };</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>There&#39;s no <code>default</code>. If you add a <code>Crypto</code> payment type later, this <code>switch</code> stops compiling until you handle it. The compiler finds every place to update, instead of your users finding the bug.</p>\n<h2 id=\"which-one-to-use\">Which One to Use</h2>\n<div data-table-scroll><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>You need…</th>\n<th>Use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>An object that only holds data</td>\n<td><code>record</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>One of a fixed list of values, maybe with data each</td>\n<td><code>enum</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>One of a fixed list of kinds, each with its own fields</td>\n<td><code>sealed interface</code> + records</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>An object whose state changes over time</td>\n<td>A regular class</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>A record is an immutable data class with constructor, accessors, <code>equals</code>, <code>hashCode</code> and <code>toString</code> built in.</li>\n<li>Validate and clean values in a record&#39;s compact constructor, so every instance is valid.</li>\n<li>Enums list a fixed set of values, can carry fields and methods, and are compared with <code>==</code>.</li>\n<li>A sealed interface lists every allowed implementation, so the compiler knows all cases.</li>\n<li><code>switch</code> with record patterns over a sealed type needs no <code>default</code> and catches missing cases at compile time.</li>\n</ol>\n"}